OK, I haven't tried to 'kick' my alpha yet with the 2.4.18 kernel and
actually only booted with it once since it hasn't been down since.

Using ext2 as FS (I'm planning to change to ext3 in the future, at least for
/) I have before seen so many fsck errors during boot after a 'kick' (I
never myself kicked it, but using IDE disks from IBM, Travelstar, with the
Multia was a bad idea so I went with much more expensive SCSI disks) that
the automatic boottime fsck wouldn't continue, but entering single user mode
and doing manual fsck always enabled me to get back and running.

I'm not sure if 2.4.17 was so good, but 2.4.18 has been rocksolid til now.
The basesystem is RH7.1.

